{"step_index":694,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-07-24T02:27:37Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now focusing on tool selection, emphasizing specific tools over general ones where possible. The goal is to optimize efficiency by leveraging tools like 'view_file' directly, rather than resorting to broader, less direct methods. I'm aiming for targeted actions.\n\n\n**Refining Image Clarity**\n\nI'm revisiting the image clarity concern raised by the user. I've focused on `PixelImage.tsx`, specifically the scaling and pixel size logic. Based on the current code, when `pixelSize` reaches 1, the image should render completely clear, as the code directly draws the full image. I'm investigating potential discrepancies between canvas dimensions and scaling, suspecting this might be the source of the perceived pixelation, despite the explicit 'clear' draw condition. I will next investigate the scaling logic in detail.\n\n\n**Addressing Retina Display Issues**\n\nI've zeroed in on the blurriness issue on high-DPI screens. I've realized that the HTML5 Canvas needs `window.devicePixelRatio` for sharpness, and if it's not applied, the resulting image appears blurry. I am revising `PixelImage.tsx` to handle this. I am now updating to incorporate the `devicePixelRatio` to the canvas.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Fix canvas resolution for Retina screens so the image ends up perfectly clear","EndLine":63,"Instruction":"Add devicePixelRatio support to the canvas dimensions and ensure it finishes exactly on pixelSize 1","ReplacementContent":"    img.onload = () => {\n      // Use devicePixelRatio to ensure Retina crispness\n      const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 2;\n      const width = canvas.clientWidth;\n      const height = canvas.clientHeight;\n      \n      canvas.width = width * dpr;\n      canvas.height = height * dpr;\n\n      const draw = (pixelSize: number) => {\n        ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n\n        // When pixelSize is 1 or less, draw the crisp high-res image\n        if (pixelSize <= 1.05) {\n          ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = true; // Enable smoothing for the crisp final photo\n          ctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n          return;\n        }\n\n        // Calculate downscaled dimensions (how many logical blocks)\n        const scaledW = Math.max(1, Math.floor(width / pixelSize));\n        const scaledH = Math.max(1, Math.floor(height / pixelSize));\n\n        // Use offscreen canvas to create the pixel data\n        const offscreen = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n        offscreen.width = scaledW;\n        offscreen.height = scaledH;\n        const offCtx = offscreen.getContext(\"2d\");\n        \n        if (offCtx) {\n          offCtx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, scaledW, scaledH);\n          \n          // Draw the tiny canvas back onto the main canvas, scaled up to fill the high-res bounds\n          ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false; // Disable smoothing to show crisp square blocks\n          ctx.drawImage(offscreen, 0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n        }\n      };\n\n      // Animate block size from 40px blocks down to 1px (sharp)\n      animationRef = animate(40, 1, {\n        duration: 0.35,\n        ease: \"circOut\",\n        onUpdate: (latest) => draw(latest),\n        onComplete: () => draw(1) // Guarantee it finishes perfectly clear\n      });\n    };","StartLine":19,"TargetContent":"    img.onload = () => {\n      // Match canvas internal resolution to its display size\n      const width = canvas.clientWidth;\n      const height = canvas.clientHeight;\n      canvas.width = width;\n      canvas.height = height;\n\n      const draw = (pixelSize: number) => {\n        ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);\n\n        if (pixelSize <= 1) {\n          ctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, width, height);\n          return;\n        }\n\n        // Calculate downscaled dimensions (how many blocks across)\n        const scaledW = Math.max(1, Math.floor(width / pixelSize));\n        const scaledH = Math.max(1, Math.floor(height / pixelSize));\n\n        // Use offscreen canvas to create the pixel data\n        const offscreen = document.createElement(\"canvas\");\n        offscreen.width = scaledW;\n        offscreen.height = scaledH;\n        const offCtx = offscreen.getContext(\"2d\");\n        \n        if (offCtx) {\n          offCtx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, scaledW, scaledH);\n          \n          // Draw the tiny canvas back onto the main canvas, scaled up\n          ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;\n          ctx.drawImage(offscreen, 0, 0, width, height);\n        }\n      };\n\n      // Animate block size from 40px blocks down to 1px (sharp)\n      animationRef = animate(40, 1, {\n        duration: 0.35,\n        ease: \"circOut\",\n        onUpdate: (latest) => draw(latest),\n      });\n    };","TargetFile":"/home/clouder/Documents/projects/buildroot/front-buildroot/components/ui/PixelImage.tsx","toolAction":"Fix canvas retina blur","toolSummary":"File edit"}}]}
