{"step_index":934,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-07-24T03:16:06Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 8 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. la intermitencia un poco mas rapida del all works\n2. un poco mas lento\n3. Perfecto, me encanta como quedo. Vamos a trabajar en la siguiente seccion, get in touch lets build... quisiera que en esta seccion pongamos un texto largo de lo que hacemos contruyendo te nologia y dise;ando soluciones, de que trabta el trabjo y en que ayuda. todo el texto grande que ocupe el espacio en x. que la letra sea thin, pero grande.\n4. primero el plan, recuerda.\n5. [Approved] plan-fase-5-cta.md\n\n6. Me gusta, pero el efecto de las letras oscureciendo va tarde. cuando el texto este 100vh  deberia estar negro todo el texto.\n7. Pero ahora no se ve el efecto que habia...\n8. Me gusta, pero igual el efecto termina tarde... cuando esta el texto en la pantalla completa, la mitadd esta negra y la otra mitad no se la lee, deberia al menos leerse hasta la 4 linea de forma clara.\n9. Hermoso. podriamos subir un poco mas esta seccion y el lets build togheter mas arriba tambien.\n10. ahora vamos a normalizar las lineas del navbar... son distintas a la que usamos al home... igualmente la distancia con los bordes. El peso de la letra de cll 7... podria ser un poco mas thin, intentar normalizar\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Normalize Navbar/Footer lines and weights:** \"normalizar las lineas del navbar... son distintas a la que usamos al home... igualmente la distancia con los bordes. El peso de la letra de cll 7... podria ser un poco mas thin\". Status: **IMPLEMENTATION** (Pending completion).\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n- **Design Philosophy:** \"Híbrido Brutalista (Crudo + Elegante)\".\n- **Typography:** Global preference for `font-light` (thin). Titles like \"Our Process\" use `capitalize` and `font-black` for specific weight.\n- **Interactions:**\n    - \"All Works\" CTA: Uses `ScrambleText` with a blinking `*` to `_` interval set to **800ms**.\n    - Scroll behavior: The manifesto text in `CTA.tsx` uses `useScroll` with `offset: [\"start 80%\", \"center center\"]` to ensure text is fully visible/dark when centered.\n- **Directives:** \"No digas de que es la app\", \"letra mas thin en el resto\", \"no uses uppercase, usa capitalize\".\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n- **Manifesto CTA (Fase 5):** Replaced static contact section with a scroll-triggered, massive-typography manifesto in `CTA.tsx`. Text reveals line-by-line using `framer-motion` scroll-scrubbing.\n- **SelectWork Refinement:** Fully aligned with brutalist standards. Removed \"Selected Work\" header, tightened spacing, changed all headings to `capitalize` (no uppercase), and added `ScrambleText` with custom blinking cursor logic to the \"All Works\" CTA.\n- **WorkflowSteps:** Updated \"Our Process\" to `text-h1`, `capitalize`, and `font-black` for maximum visual weight.\n- **Typography:** Global enforcement of `font-light` for body and secondary headers.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Scroll Logic:** Resolved \"reveal delay\" issues by shifting `useScroll` offset to `[\"start 80%\", \"center center\"]`. This ensures the animation completes exactly when the element is centered in the viewport.\n- **Component State:** The blinking cursor logic (`*` to `_`) is implemented via `useEffect` with `setInterval` at 800ms to avoid excessive flickering.\n- **Constraints:** Canvas-based pixelation (`PixelImage.tsx`) requires careful handling of internal dimensions on high-DPI displays.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files:**\n    - `/home/clouder/Documents/projects/buildroot/front-buildroot/components/home/SelectWork.tsx`: Cleaned heade