{"step_index":2405,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-07-25T21:31:10Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 22 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. en la navbar existe etexto en espanol... todo en ingles y en la ruta /es en espalin... o como lo manejamos?\n2. la idea es que sea en ingles y tengamos la posibilidad de mostrar tambien el contenido en espanol para clientes locales.\n3. /plan\n4. [Approved] i18n-implementation-plan.md\n[Approved] plan-fase-5-cta.md\n\n5. bueno, ahora si agrega el contenido en espanol para poder cambiarlo y verlo. tambien el boton de ES no cambia a EN\n6. Podrias revisar porque esta en internal server error\n7. Tengo doss observaciones. No aparece el modulo de projectos del home que arreglamos, y tambien las tarjetgas del our process, eran cinco si no estoy mal. '\n8. ejecuta nuevamente porque tengo un error\n9. No, no era ese el contenido ni color de las tarjetas, revisa las anteriores.. y el selected work, cambiamos el estilo a featured works, y no trae eso... estamos con mu moduolo viejo.\n10. No, no, no y no... eso no fue lo que hicimos antes de lo de cambiar el idioma.\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Restore original \"Our Process\" (WorkflowSteps) design:** User explicitly rejected the current implementation, demanding a return to the brutalist, grid-based, border-heavy design that existed prior to the recent refactoring.\n  - *Status: IMPLEMENTATION*\n- **Restore original \"Featured Projects\" (WorkSection) design:** User demands the original grid-based `WorkSection` (which used a `ProjectsGrid` component) instead of the current, simplified, or \"wrong\" module being displayed.\n  - *Status: IMPLEMENTATION*\n- **\"No, no, no y no... eso no fue lo que hicimos antes de lo de cambiar el idioma\":** The user is highly dissatisfied with recent regressions caused by `git checkout` operations that wiped their local visual customizations.\n  - *Status: IMPLEMENTATION (Priority 1)*\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n- **Design Philosophy:** \"Híbrido Brutalista (Crudo + Elegante)\". The user has a very high sensitivity to visual regressions (color, grid layout, card spacing).\n- **Language Strategy:** English as default (hidden); Spanish requires `/es/` prefix.\n- **Key Directives:**\n  - \"No, no era ese el contenido ni color de las tarjetas, revisa las anteriores.\"\n  - \"El selected work, cambiamos el estilo a featured works, y no trae eso... estamos con mi modulo viejo.\"\n  - The user expects the \"Our Process\" component to have exactly five cards (Discovery, Architecture, Build, Ship, Optimization).\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n- **I18n Foundations:** Established dictionary-driven localization for core components.\n- **Environment:** Resolved recurring Turbopack/Next.js `ENOENT` / 500 errors by clearing `.next/` and managing port collisions (port 3000 now stable).\n- **Failed Restoration:** Attempted to restore the desired state via `git checkout ac51666`, which restored older code but inadvertently reverted subsequent i18n and content updates, leading to the user's current frustration.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture & Interfaces:**\n  - `app/[lang]/page.tsx` acts as the server-side controller for language data, passing `dict` objects down to client components.\n- **Failures:**\n  - `git checkout` on specific files is dangerous when local modifications are not committed, as it pulls state from the tree that overwrites recent progress without warning.\n  - Next.js 16/Turbopack in this environment frequently requires `fuser -k 3000/tcp` and a full `.next` purge to resolve `ENOENT` errors.\n- **Component Anatomy:** The user prefers the `WorkSection` that uses the `Highlights` grid style, not the currently active horizontal card implementation.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files:**\n  - `/home/clouder/Documents/projects/buildroot/front-buildroot/components/home/WorkflowSteps.tsx`: Currently modified to accept `dict` props but has a regressed grid layout; needs to be synced with the visual \"brutalist\" standard.\n  - `/home/clouder/Documents/projects/buildroot/front-buildroot/app/[lang]/page.tsx`: Updated to switch between `WorkSection` and `SelectWork`.\n- **Relevant Files:**\n  - `components/home/WorkflowSteps.tsx`: Restoration point for the grid-border design.\n  - `components/work/WorkSection.tsx` / `components/home/Highlights.tsx`: Need to verify these contain the correct \"Featured Works\" grid structure the user expects.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Immediate Next Step:** Re-integrate the desired visual layouts (the grid-border `WorkflowSteps` and the \"Featured Works\" grid) while *preserving* the `dict` prop implementation for localization. \n- **Guidance:** Do not use `git checkout` to restore files. Instead, manually identify the code differences from previous working states (if accessible via history logs) and port them into the existing localized components.\n- **User Instruction:** \"No, no, no y no... eso no fue lo que hicimos antes de lo de cambiar el idioma.\" (The user expects the specific visual polish/design finalized *before* the language-toggle feature was integrated).\n- **Skills/Rules:** The `.agents/rules/core.md` defines the project identity (brutalist, tech venture). Refer to it for styling cues.\n\nYou have the 7 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: aca_diario_1784858012774]\nPath: file:///home/clouder/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/74f699fd-4686-4bd7-8785-781c4ec34204/aca_diario_1784858012774.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-07-24T01:53:32Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: edusur_1784857998587]\nPath: file:///home/clouder/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/74f699fd-4686-4bd7-8785-781c4e